"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 21784, "like_count": 113, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 16}, "text": "🔥🔥🔥\n\n\"Both the headline and core are higher than expected and, critically, core met the threshold that Fed Governor Waller laid out for a larger 50 bps rate hike.\"\n\nhttps://t.co/kSULJJav9d", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120147968468955555"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:33:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120147923157540959"], "id": "2120147923157540959", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 26959, "like_count": 117, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "As a reminder, there will be no y/y CPI reading given the government shutdown a year ago when CPI wasn’t released", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120147923157540959"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:33:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120147833906934250"], "id": "2120147833906934250", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 15947, "like_count": 96, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "In m/m terms, October CPI #inflation +0.4% vs. +0.3% est. &amp; +0.6% prior … core CPI +0.3% vs. +0.2% est. &amp; +0.3% prior https://t.co/ATg0HYhrNy", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120147833906934250"}, {"author_id": "188369814", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:04:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120140578042310945"], "id": "2120140578042310945", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 30536, "like_count": 180, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 51, "retweet_count": 25}, "text": "In the last 2+ weeks, Brent Crude Oil (blue) has declined 22%, from $116.72 on October 23rd to $90.56 today.\n\nBut the 10-year yield (black) has declined by only 10 basis points (from 4.99% on Oct 23 to 4.89% today).\n\nThe bond market is NOT about crude prices. https://t.co/ITS2sBhVLV", "url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2120140578042310945"}, {"author_id": "3311286493", "created_at": "2026-11-10T13:02:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120140062872813800"], "id": "2120140062872813800", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 16, "impression_count": 25981, "like_count": 191, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "一 个美女 间 谍\nNot often that intermediate vocab is this topical!", "url": "https://x.com/adam_tooze/status/2120140062872813800"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:49:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120136641511653625"], "id": "2120136641511653625", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2502, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119437625639551342", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Sadly for everyone, I'm not Neil Dutta, but I had the opportunity to pinch-hit for him on last week's RenMac Off-Script podcast.  \n\nVery grateful to Neil, Jeff DeGraaf, and the rest of the RenMac team for having me on! https://t.co/68WhrrX7ZM", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120136641511653625"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:30:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131944952602743"], "id": "2120131944952602743", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 12904, "like_count": 50, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120130654704894051", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "\"Federal Reserve Governor Christopher Waller on Tuesday said he supports an interest-rate hike in December, and warned that if inflation continues to accelerate he would support a half-percentage-point increase to protect the central bank’s credibility.\"\n\nhttps://t.co/U21GDe9kVw https://t.co/KtQwjazJRC", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120131944952602743"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:29:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131755512623249"], "id": "2120131755512623249", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 15618, "like_count": 64, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Quality of labor was cited as the single most important problem for small businesses for the fourth consecutive month in October, followed by taxes, which overtook inflation, according to @NFIB https://t.co/07taA6jFeZ", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120131755512623249"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:29:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131663879401863"], "id": "2120131663879401863", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17340, "like_count": 47, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "October @NFIB Small Business Optimism slipped to 97.8 vs. 98.2 est. &amp; 97.9 prior https://t.co/TO85S6g9hk", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120131663879401863"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:28:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131534174761356"], "id": "2120131534174761356", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 14300, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "Last Wednesday’s post-election rout saw S&amp;P 500 drop 4.3% and NASDAQ 100 decline 6.4% ... since then they are up 2.7% and 4.8%, respectively and both are up over 10% YTD \n[Past performance is no guarantee of future results.] https://t.co/mQqeabcvO1", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120131534174761356"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:27:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131230289305622"], "id": "2120131230289305622", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 14226, "like_count": 40, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Global food prices, as tracked byFAO (Food &amp; Agriculture Organization) Price Index, dipped in October … index was nearly 6% higher than a year ago but 16% below its March peak … prices for vegetable oils and sugars increased while cereals, meats and dairy prices fell https://t.co/OJE3Andv3K", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120131230289305622"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:26:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120131062563029252"], "id": "2120131062563029252", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 16622, "like_count": 91, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "Share of consumers citing an erosion in their living standards due to higher prices rose to 57% in November, matching May’s record reading, according to latest @UMich Consumer Sentiment Survey https://t.co/sUvGZ8okOZ", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120131062563029252"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:26:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120130990043795964"], "id": "2120130990043795964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 35970, "like_count": 238, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 23, "retweet_count": 20}, "text": "*ANTHROPIC SEEKS $1.4 TRILLION FULLY DILUTED VALUATION IN IPO", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120130990043795964"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-10T12:26:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120130889271402638"], "id": "2120130889271402638", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 15161, "like_count": 66, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "According to Bloomberg, mentions of “inflation” or “inflationary” on S&amp;P 500 earnings calls jumped to 820 in October, the highest monthly total since February 2024 … industrial companies accounted for a quarter of those mentions, followed by the Materials sector https://t.co/1Nrc3s6fs6", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2120130889271402638"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "188369